<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Melchor Pacheco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Melchor Pacheco was a Spanish conquistador who, with his kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-pacheco">Gaspar Pacheco</a>, led the conquest of the eastern provinces of Yucatán in 1544. Their campaigns against Uaymil, Cochuah and Chetumal were notorious for their cruelty, and the region was largely depopulated. The conquered lands became part of the Province of Yucatán.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/melchor-pacheco.jpg" alt="Melchor Pacheco" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cuilomerto (photograph); Creator:Fernando Castro Pacheco (mural) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_conquista.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
